        "path": "services/runtime.py",
        "end_line": 38,
        "start_line": 33
      },
      {
        "path": "services/runtime.py",
        "end_line": 24,
        "start_line": 24
      }
    ],
    "patch_decision": "NO_CODE_PATCH",
    "recommended_fix": "Replace the per-product detail lookups in inventory-service with a single set-based query (fetch all products for the page in one statement, e.g. reuse the existing `SELECT id,name,price,stock FROM products ORDER BY id LIMIT $1` result or use `WHERE id = ANY($1)`), eliminating the N+1 loop. This reduces DB round-trips and pool connection churn. Not fixable within the allowlisted pricing.py scope, so no code patch is applied here; route the inventory-service handler change to the owner.",
    "affected_service": "inventory-service",
    "reasoning_summary": "Two independent evidence types converge. (1) DB statement stats (E-d08c02695db84f15): per-id products query 56,920 calls / 56,920 rows = 1 query per row vs 1,683 batched calls, the defining N+1 ratio. (2) inventory-service pool stats (E-765c47c7853244e2): requests_num 60,976 closely matches combined call count, with requests_queued=490, requests_wait_ms=294,308 and 248 errors indicating connection contention. runtime.py (E-b7f6ea5c788a45dc) shows query() takes a fresh pool connection per call with pool max_size=4, explaining how per-row queries saturate the pool. HTTP metrics (E-fe5264e520694240) show inventory db_qps ~7.8 tracking request throughput with 0% errors, so the impact is DB/pool amplification, not per-request errors. pg_sleep rows are not on the products path (unrelated calls_delta), so they are not the root cause.",
    "remaining_uncertainty": [
      "The inventory-service request handler source is not in the allowlisted files, so the exact loop issuing per-id queries could not be read directly; the N+1 is inferred from statement call/row counts and pool stats.",
      "The 248 pool requests_errors are consistent with connection contention but the specific error code was not directly observed.",
      "pg_sleep statements (mean ~2.0s/1.2s) exist in the DB but show unrelated deltas and were not tied to the products path; their origin/owner is unconfirmed."
    ]
  },
